{:fh/id  "FH-SUB-003"
 :fh/law "A candidate rendered against a body revision the cell has since replaced is stale and publishes nothing — checked both at commit entry and again at the narrowest publication boundary, after the callback-capable staging work."

 :query [:shell/v]

 ;; Point 1: the reload lands in the render→commit gap. The live cell
 ;; keeps exactly the dependency set its own body earned.
 :entry-fence {:result           :abandoned
               :generation       1
               :lifecycle        :connected
               :dependency-count 1
               :ref-count        1}

 ;; Point 2: the reload lands INSIDE the commit. A cold site's body runs
 ;; twice — once for the render's pure probe, once for the node the
 ;; commit installs — so reloading on the second run is a reload that
 ;; lands after currency was first checked.
 :publication-fence {:reload-on-computation 2
                     :result                :abandoned
                     :generation            1
                     :lifecycle             :new
                     :dependency-count      0
                     :ref-count             nil}}
